theorem shrinkerEntropyData_F_value (n : ℕ) (τ : ℝ) (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    EntropyData.F (shrinkerEntropyData n τ hτ) = (n : ℝ) / (2 * τ) := by
  unfold EntropyData.F shrinkerEntropyData
  -- F = ∫ (0 + ‖x‖²/(4τ²)) * K n τ x = ∫ (1/(4τ²)) * (‖x‖² * K)
  have hfun : (fun x : Euc n => (0 + shrinkerGradSq τ x) * gaussianKernel n τ x) =
      fun x => (1 / (4 * τ ^ 2)) * (‖x‖ ^ 2 * gaussianKernel n τ x) := by
    funext x; rw [shrinkerGradSq]; ring
  rw [hfun, integral_const_mul, integral_normSq_mul_gaussianKernel n hτ]
  field_simp [sq_nonneg (τ) ... ] -- (1/(4τ²))·(2nτ) = n/(2τ): field_simp [hτ.ne'] — 4τ² = 2τ·2τ... (1/(4τ²))·(2nτ): field_simp [pow_ne_zero 2 hτ.ne']; ring
```
`integral_const_mul` needs Integrable — from integrable_normSq_mul_gaussianKernel n hτ ✓ (as an explicit arg or auto-inferred? `integral_const_mul r f hf` — hf explicit). Actually signature: `theorem integral_const_mul (r : 𝕜) (f : α → E) (hf : Integrable f μ)`. So `rw [hfun, integral_const_mul (1/(4*τ^2)) (fun x => ‖x‖²*K n τ x) (integrable_normSq_mul_gaussianKernel n hτ), integral_normSq_mul_gaussianKernel n hτ]`.

W value: W = τF + extra, extra = ∫(f - n)ρ = ∫(‖x‖²/(4τ) - n)K = (1/(4τ))·2nτ - n·1 = n/2 - n = -n/2. W = τ·(n/(2τ)) - n/2 = n/2 - n/2 = 0.
```
theorem shrinkerEntropyData_W_value (n : ℕ) (τ : ℝ) (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    EntropyData.W (shrinkerEntropyData n τ hτ) = 0 := by
  rw [EntropyData.W_eq]  -- W = τ*F + extra
  rw [shrinkerEntropyData_F_value n τ hτ]
  unfold EntropyData.extra shrinkerEntropyData
  -- extra = ∫ (‖x‖²/(4τ) - n) * K
  have hfun : (fun x : Euc n => (shrinkerFpot τ x - (n : ℝ)) * gaussianKernel n τ x) =
      fun x => (1 / (4 * τ)) * (‖x‖ ^ 2 * gaussianKernel n τ x) - (n : ℝ) * gaussianKernel n τ x := by
    funext x; rw [shrinkerFpot]; ring
  rw [hfun, integral_sub, integral_const_mul, integral_normSq_mul_gaussianKernel n hτ, integral_const_mul, gaussianKernel_integral n hτ]
  field_simp [hτ.ne']
  ring
```
integral_sub needs Integrable of both: integrable_normSq_mul_gaussianKernel n hτ, integrable_gaussianKernel n hτ. `integral_const_mul (n:ℝ) (fun x => K n τ x) (integrable_gaussianKernel n hτ)`.

